ISSUE 0653 IS YOURS, for when Intent is called. hv ruled on 2026-10-26, by TUI in molt-vc's session, that intent-dc builds it in 3.2.7. It puts hv's verblock rule into Intent: "THE VERBLOCK IS NOT A REPLACEMENT FOR VERSION CONTROL. DO NOT STORE PROSE IN THE VERBLOCK. Just the docs version and a short -- no more than 1-line -- text about the current version." The ruling is in 0653's record and on vc's board as a decision. Read the record first.

The bank carries:
- a library rule, IN-PR-STYLE-005, holding hv's words verbatim;
- verblock-guard.sh, beside staged-format-guard.sh, on STAGED markdown only, refusing a second version stamp or a quoted value longer than 100 characters, with one red and one green arm per refusal;
- two pointer lines that cite the rule's ID (the Markdown line of lib/templates/llm/_AGENTS.md, and in-finish's wip.md step);
- AGENTS.md regenerated, the CHANGELOG line and the MODULES row, registered before code.

It is going-forward only, so records are left as they are. The template and the guard are live on save in every estate, so build in a detached worktree, bank it, and book the judge with molt-vc in Intent's train.

Your own EOD files from 2026-10-25 are still uncommitted: board.json, wip.md, and two event files. vc re-created board.json from the store on hv's (b) at 06:20Z, with heartbeat 20:00:29.487Z, and committed none of them. Commit them at your pickup. No push, no release.
